\
----------------------------------------------\
\uc0\u55358 \u56800  Project Overview\
----------------------------------------------\
Warrensburg Clothing Store is a simple full-stack web application built using\
Java Spring Boot microservices for the backend and React.js for the frontend.\
It demonstrates CRUD operations, database integration (H2), and microservice\
communication in a real-world online retail context.\
\
The system allows:\
- Customers to register/login, browse products, and manage a cart.\
- Admin to manage products and view customers.\
- All data stored in persistent H2 SQL databases.\
\
----------------------------------------------\
\uc0\u55356 \u57303 \u65039  System Architecture\
----------------------------------------------\
The project follows a **Microservices Architecture**.\
\
Each service runs independently on a different port:\
\
1\uc0\u65039 \u8419  **Customer Service (port 8082)**\
   - Manages customer registration, login, and authentication.\
   - Stores customer data in H2 database (customerdb).\
   - Supports role-based access (ADMIN / CUSTOMER).\
   - Exposes REST endpoints for:\
     - POST /register\
     - POST /login\
     - GET /customers\
     - DELETE /customers/\{id\}\
\
2\uc0\u65039 \u8419  **Product Service (port 8081)**\
   - Manages product catalog and shopping cart.\
   - Performs all CRUD operations on products.\
   - Stores data in H2 database (productdb).\
   - Exposes REST endpoints for:\
     - GET /products\
     - POST /products\
     - PUT /products/\{id\}\
     - DELETE /products/\{id\}\
     - GET /cart\
     - POST /cart/add\
     - DELETE /cart/\{id\}\
\
3\uc0\u65039 \u8419  **React Frontend (port 3000 or 3001+)**\
   - Connects to both microservices via REST APIs.\
   - Has two login paths: Customer and Admin.\
   - Customer:\
       \uc0\u8594  Registers/logs in and views products.\
       \uc0\u8594  Adds/removes items in the shopping cart.\
   - Admin:\
       \uc0\u8594  Manages (Add/Edit/Delete) products.\
       \uc0\u8594  Views customer list.\
\
----------------------------------------------\
\uc0\u55357 \u56510  Database Design\
----------------------------------------------\
H2 databases (SQL-based) are used for persistence.\
\
\uc0\u55358 \u56781  Customer DB (customerdb)\
   Table: CUSTOMER\
   Columns:\
     - ID (Primary Key)\
     - NAME\
     - EMAIL\
     - PASSWORD_HASH\
     - ROLE (ADMIN or CUSTOMER)\
\
\uc0\u55357 \u56405  Product DB (productdb)\
   Tables:\
     - PRODUCT (ID, NAME, PRICE, STOCK)\
     - CART (ID, CUSTOMER_ID)\
     - CART_ITEM (ID, CART_ID, PRODUCT_ID, QUANTITY, PRICE, PRODUCT_NAME)\
\
Each CRUD operation (Create, Read, Update, Delete) can be demonstrated\
through the UI or via the H2 console.\
\
----------------------------------------------\
\uc0\u55357 \u56741 \u65039  CRUD Demonstration Guide\
----------------------------------------------\
\uc0\u9989  CREATE\
- Admin adds a new product in the Admin Dashboard.\
- Customer registers with new credentials.\
\
\uc0\u9989  READ\
- Product and customer lists display automatically in the UI.\
- You can also run SQL:\
  SELECT * FROM PRODUCT;  SELECT * FROM CUSTOMER;\
\
\uc0\u9989  UPDATE\
- Admin can edit product name, price, or stock.\
- Customer can add items to cart (updates cart table).\
\
\uc0\u9989  DELETE\
- Admin can delete products.\
- Customer can remove items from cart.\
\
----------------------------------------------\
\uc0\u55356 \u57256  Frontend Overview\
----------------------------------------------\
- Built with React (Functional Components + Hooks)\
- Uses Fetch API to call microservices.\
- Clean UI with login pages for Admin & Customer.\
- Simple cart and product management system.\
\
Pages:\
  1. Login Page (Admin / Customer choice)\
  2. Product List Page\
  3. Cart Page\
  4. Admin Dashboard\
\
